  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Finnish investor Tomas von Rettig spent five years in Germany as a professional show jumper, joining Ludger Beerbaum's team at eighteen. He later returned to Finland to study finance and began working outside the family business at SEB. He regarded joining the family firm as his own decision, rather than an obligation.\n\nWhile still at the bank, he joined a programme designed to introduce interested family members to the group's businesses. His father and former chief executive Bjarne Mitts helped teach him. Once responsible for corporate finance, he prioritised competing investment needs and used external advisers alongside internal analysis to monitor markets.",
